        {
            "input": {
                "level": "0", 
                "op": "log_level"
            }, 
            "expected_output": "{\"error\":\"unknown_log_level\",\"status\":\"error\"}\n"
        }
    ], 
    "description": "Resolve a human-supplied log-level label to a canonical severity. Matching is case-insensitive and surrounding whitespace is ignored. Recognized labels include trace, debug, info, warn (alias warning), error (alias err) and notice (treated as info). An empty or whitespace-only label defaults to info. Any unrecognized label is reported as an error category."
